          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classical mathematics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+spaces"} metric spaces
            with their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+topology"} metric topology
            it is true that
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequentially+compact+metric+spaces+are+equivalently+compact+metric+spaces"} sequentially compact metric spaces are equivalently compact metric spaces
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequentially+compact+topological+space"} sequentially compact
            in general neither implies nor is implied by being
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
            (see the counter-examples
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "sequentially+compact+topological+space#Examples"} here
          %p
            But the failure of this equivalence is not due to a deficit in the concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convergence"} convergence
            but in the concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequences"} sequences
            and sub-sequences. If the latter are generalized to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nets"} nets
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sub-nets"} sub-nets
            (beware that the definition of sub-nets is slightly non-obvious), then the analogue of the statement remains true in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classical mathematics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
            precisely if every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/net"} net
            in it has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sub-net"} sub-net
            that
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/converges"} converges
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/law+of+excluded+middle"} law of excluded middle
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/law+of+excluded+middle"} law of excluded middle
          %h2#statement Statement
          #CompactSpacesEquivalentlyHaveConvergetSubnets.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong (compact spaces are equivalently those for which every net has a converging subnet)
            %p
              Assuming
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
              and the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
              precisely if every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/net"} net
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sub-net"} sub-net
              that
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convergence"} converges
          %p
            We break this up into lemmas
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InACompactSpaceEveryNetHasAConvergentSubnet"}
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#IfEveryNetHasConvergentSubnetThenSpaceIsCompact"}
          #InACompactSpaceEveryNetHasAConvergentSubnet.num_example
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              %strong (in a compact space, every net has a convergent subnet)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              has a convergent subnet.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ν
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu \colon A \to X
              be a net. We need to show that there is a subnet which converges.
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
              consider the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+closures"} topological closures
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(S_a)
              of the sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_a
              of elements of the net beyond some fixed index:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi a
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %msub
                        %mi ν
                        %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi b
                      %mo ≥
                      %mi a
                      %mo }
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S_a
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\left\{
                    \\nu_b  \in X \;\vert\; b \geq a
                    \\right\}
                    \\subset X
                    \\,.
            %p
              Observe that the set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi a
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{S_a \subset X\}_{a \in A}
              and hence also the set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{Cl(S_a) \subset X\}_{a \in A}
              has the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+intersection+property"} finite intersection property
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+set"} directed set
              %a{:href => "finite+intersection+property#CompactnessInTermsOfFiniteIntersectionProperty"} this prop.
              implies from the assumption of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              being compact that the intersection of
              %em all
              the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(S_a)
              is non-empty, hence that there is an element
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %munder
                      %mo ∩
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi A
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    x \in \underset{a \in A}{\cap}  Cl(S_a)
                    \\,.
            %p
              In particular every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighbourhood"} neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              intersects each of the
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(S_a)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_a
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
              there exists
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ≥
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \geq a
              such that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ν
                        %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu_b \in U_x
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cluster+point"} cluster point
              of the net.
            %p
              We will now produce a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sub-net"} sub-net
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mi ν
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    B &amp;&amp; \overset{f}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp; A
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\nu}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; X
                    }
            %p
              that converges to this cluster point. To this end, we first need to build the domain directed set
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              with the directed neighbourhood set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Nbhd
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Nbhd_X(x)
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo ≤
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi Nbhd
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊃
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    B \subset A_{\leq} \times Nbhd_X(x)_{\supset}
            %p on those pairs such that the element of the net indexed by the first component is is contained in the second component:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi ν
                        %mi a
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi X
                      %mo }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    B
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\left\{
                    (a,U_x)  \,\vert \, \nu_a \in U_X
                    \\right\}
                    \\,.
            %p
              It is clear
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preordered+set"} preordered set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_1, U_1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_2, U_2)
              has a common upper bound
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi bd
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi bd
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_{bd}, U_{bd})
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              itself is directed, there is an upper bound
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 3
                      %mo ≥
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_3 \geq a_1, a_2
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              is a cluster point of the net there is moreover an
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi bd
                    %mo ≥
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 3
                    %mo ≥
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_{bd} \geq a_3 \geq a_1, a_3
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ν
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi a
                            %mi bd
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu_{a_{bd}} \in U_1 \cap U_2
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi bd
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{bd} \coloneqq U_1 \cap U_2
              we have obtained the required pair.
            %p
              Next take the function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              to be given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi a
                            %mo ,
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ↦
                              %mphantom
                                %mi AAA
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    B &amp;\overset{f}{\longrightarrow}&amp; A
                    \\\
                    (a, U) &amp;\overset{\phantom{AAA}}{\mapsto}&amp; a
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is clearly order preserving, and it is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofinal"} cofinal
              since it is even a surjection. Hence we have defined a subnet
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ν
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu \circ f
            %p
              It now remains to see that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ν
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu \circ f
              converges to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              we may find
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,U)
              such that for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (b,V)
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \leq b
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊃
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \supset V
              then
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ν
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi ν
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu(f(b,V)) = \nu(b) \in U_x
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              there exists some
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              with
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ν
                        %mi a
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu_a \in U_x
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \coloneqq U_x
              then nature of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              implies that with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi V
